      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. I need you to confirm the dose first.\n\n**Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is 5 times the maximum recommended dose.** For adults, amlodipine is usually started at 2.5\u20135 mg once daily and topped out at 10 mg once daily. Going above that can cause severe low blood pressure, shock and swelling that's hard to treat, and the drug's long half-life makes an overdose harder to manage.\n\nThis looks like it might be a typo for **5 mg** (one less zero), which is a common starting dose.\n\nCould you confirm which you meant?\n- **Amlodipine 5 mg by mouth, once daily**, or\n- **Amlodipine 10 mg by mouth, once daily**, or\n- Another dose within the usual range\n\nIf you really do want a dose above 10 mg, please tell me why and I'll note it on the order. I'd still suggest checking with pharmacy before it goes through."
      }
