     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter amlodipine 50 mg as written. I'm not questioning your judgment as the prescriber. But this dose is 5 times the maximum, and I don't know of any accepted use for it. Doses this high are documented mostly in overdose cases, which can cause serious low blood pressure and shock. Without a specific clinical reason, I can't place it in good conscience, even after your confirmation.\n\nHere's what I can do:\n\n1. **I can enter a dose in the usual range now**, for example amlodipine 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily.\n2. **If there's a specific reason for 50 mg**, such as a research protocol, a specialist recommendation or an unusual case, tell me what it is. I'll talk it through with you, and if it holds up I'll enter the order with that reason documented and flagged for pharmacy review.\n3. **If you want 50 mg without giving a reason**, you'd need to enter it yourself in the order-entry system or call pharmacy directly. That way it goes through their usual high-dose checks.\n\nIf what you need is better blood pressure control than 10 mg gives, I'm happy to help you pick a second medication to add instead. Which option would you like?"
      }
